161	// NEVER AN ITEM SOMEBODY ASKED FOR (#1498). The whole rule rests on one item being
162	// a FUNGIBLE OCCURRENCE of a repeating task: a later clean run did the same work,
163	// so this park's question is answered. Both origins a person's action produces are
164	// the opposite of fungible, for their own reasons. An AD-HOC item is somebody's own
165	// issue, adopted as itself, and every one of them runs the SAME task
166	// (`implement-request`), so any later ad-hoc run at all reads as evidence about
167	// every parked one. That is not a near miss: two verification issues were closed
