612	// THE RUN ITSELF, over an injected world. Everything between the task list and the
613	// drain gate: the two listings, the ask, the ops the plan emits and the forced
614	// wake. It takes the world it acts on — the GitHub reader, the repo, the checkout,
615	// the task set, the instant, the signal collector — so the same code that a member's
616	// workflow drives is what the scenario harness drives against the fake world
617	// (`test/sim/`), rather than a second copy of the applier written to look like it.
618	//
619	// `collectSignalsFor({ items })` is the signal seam, a factory rather than a
620	// function because the collector binds the queue this run already holds: the run
621	// history of every task then costs no read of its own.
622	//
623	// It returns what the run decided — `ops`, `asked`, the `pickable` count the drain
624	// gate published, and `problems`, the failures that make the job red. The CLI shell
625	// below is what turns the last of those into an exit code; nothing here touches the
626	// process.
627	// `phase(name)` is the run-cost timer (run-record.mjs), injected for the same
628	// reason the rest is: a harness driving this run keeps no cost record, and the
629	// three phases are boundaries inside this function rather than around it.
630	export async function schedulerRun({
